== 1.9 Chapter 1 Practice Drill — 40 Questions

40 questions graded in the order the CBT engine is likely to meet them. Allow 44 minutes; the key and a full solution for every question follow.

#mcq(1, [Agriculture is best defined as the],
  [study of the soil and its fertility],
  [growing of crops for food only],
  [processing of farm produce for sale],
  [science and art of cultivating crops and rearing animals]
)

#mcq(2, [The branch of agriculture that deals with field crops such as maize and sorghum is],
  [agricultural economics],
  [horticulture],
  [agronomy],
  [animal science]
)

#mcq(3, [Which of the following is NOT a branch of agriculture?],
  [animal science],
  [agronomy],
  [soil science],
  [meteorology]
)

#mcq(4, [The branch that studies the transfer of research findings to the farmer is],
  [animal husbandry],
  [soil science],
  [agronomy],
  [extension education]
)

#mcq(5, [The study of fruits, vegetables and ornamentals is called],
  [agronomy],
  [forestry],
  [horticulture],
  [fishery]
)

#mcq(6, [Agriculture is important to Nigeria mainly because it],
  [needs no capital],
  [is practised only in villages],
  [earns more than oil],
  [provides food, employment and raw materials]
)

#mcq(7, [Which of these is a raw material supplied by agriculture to industry?],
  [cement for building],
  [crude oil for refining],
  [iron ore for steel],
  [cotton for textiles]
)

#mcq(8, [A farm is described as a system because it has],
  [no management],
  [only crops],
  [inputs, processes and outputs],
  [only animals]
)

#mcq(9, [Farming carried out mainly to feed the farmer's household is],
  [mixed farming],
  [commercial farming],
  [plantation agriculture],
  [subsistence farming]
)

#mcq(10, [A farmer who grows crops and keeps animals on the same holding practises],
  [mixed cropping],
  [shifting cultivation],
  [mixed farming],
  [monoculture]
)

#mcq(11, [The growing of two or more crops together on the same plot in one season is],
  [crop rotation],
  [land rotation],
  [continuous cropping],
  [mixed cropping]
)

#mcq(12, [A fixed sequence of different crops on the same land season after season is],
  [mixed cropping],
  [shifting cultivation],
  [crop rotation],
  [plantation agriculture]
)

#mcq(13, [A farmer clears a fresh plot each year and returns to the first after about ten years. He practises],
  [mixed farming],
  [shifting cultivation],
  [continuous cropping],
  [crop rotation]
)

#mcq(14, [Land rotation differs from shifting cultivation because land rotation],
  [never rests the land],
  [follows a fixed order of plots],
  [is a form of plantation],
  [uses no fallow at all]
)

#mcq(15, [Growing the same crop on the same land every year is],
  [crop rotation],
  [strip cropping],
  [continuous cropping],
  [mixed cropping]
)

#mcq(16, [A large estate growing one cash crop with capital and hired labour is a],
  [peasant holding],
  [plantation],
  [shifting plot],
  [communal farm]
)

#mcq(17, [Which of these is an arable enterprise?],
  [cattle rearing],
  [maize production],
  [poultry keeping],
  [fish farming]
)

#mcq(18, [Pastoral farming is the rearing of],
  [fish],
  [field crops],
  [animals],
  [garden crops]
)

#mcq(19, [The rearing of fish in ponds and cages is called],
  [aquaculture],
  [horticulture],
  [agroforestry],
  [pastoralism]
)

#mcq(20, [Trees grown together with crops on the same land is],
  [agroforestry],
  [shifting cultivation],
  [mixed cropping],
  [plantation agriculture]
)

#mcq(21, [The most intensive type of farming among the following is],
  [shifting cultivation],
  [extensive cattle grazing],
  [horticulture under irrigation],
  [bush fallow]
)

#mcq(22, [Which of these is a problem of Nigerian agriculture rather than a solution?],
  [fertiliser subsidy],
  [rural feeder roads],
  [improved seed varieties],
  [fragmented and scattered holdings]
)

#mcq(23, [Land fragmentation is a problem mainly because it],
  [makes plots too small and scattered for efficient work],
  [increases soil fertility],
  [reduces the cost of inputs],
  [improves drainage]
)

#mcq(24, [The use of a hoe instead of a tractor is best described as],
  [a soil conservation measure],
  [a form of mechanisation],
  [a crude implement limiting the area a farmer can prepare],
  [an irrigation practice]
)

#mcq(25, [Which of these would most directly raise the yield of a smallholding?],
  [more land of the same quality],
  [a larger barn],
  [improved seed, fertiliser and timely planting],
  [more family labour alone]
)

#mcq(26, [Agricultural credit is a problem for the small farmer because],
  [banks pay too much interest on savings],
  [the harvest is sold too early],
  [land is too fertile],
  [inputs must be bought before any income arrives]
)

#mcq(27, [The main reason a farmer stores grain rather than selling at harvest is to],
  [increase the moisture content],
  [avoid paying for bags],
  [attract insects],
  [sell later when prices rise]
)

#mcq(28, [Poor rural roads affect agriculture chiefly by],
  [making the soil acidic],
  [reducing rainfall],
  [raising the cost of moving inputs and produce],
  [increasing seed viability]
)

#mcq(29, [Agriculture contributes to Nigeria's economy by],
  [employing a large share of the workforce],
  [replacing the oil sector entirely],
  [ending rural-urban migration],
  [removing the need for imports]
)

#mcq(30, [A crop grown mainly for sale rather than for home use is a],
  [cash crop],
  [forage crop],
  [food crop],
  [cover crop]
)

#mcq(31, [Which of these best defines a farm's 'output'?],
  [the product and the by-products of the season],
  [the seed bought before planting],
  [the land on which the crop stands],
  [the labour hired for weeding]
)

#mcq(32, [The feedback in a farm system refers to],
  [the fertiliser applied to the crop],
  [what the farmer learns and applies to the next season],
  [the rain that falls on the plot],
  [the price paid at the market]
)

#mcq(33, [Monoculture is best described as],
  [the growing of a single crop over a large area],
  [a rotation of three crops],
  [the rearing of one animal species only],
  [two crops on one plot]
)

#mcq(34, [The branch that would answer the question 'is it better to store or to sell now?' is],
  [agronomy],
  [agricultural economics],
  [plant pathology],
  [soil science]
)

#mcq(35, [Which practice best reduces the risk of total crop failure on a smallholding?],
  [growing several crops and keeping some animals],
  [using more fertiliser on one plot],
  [borrowing to hire a tractor],
  [planting one improved variety only]
)

#mcq(36, [The term 'agribusiness' covers],
  [farming only],
  [only the rearing of animals],
  [only the export trade],
  [farming plus the input supply, processing and marketing around it]
)

#mcq(37, [Which of these is a social benefit of agriculture to a rural community?],
  [income that keeps families in the village],
  [the loss of local markets],
  [an increase in urban crime],
  [a rise in soil acidity]
)

#mcq(38, [A farmer who sells his groundnut to a cooperative rather than a village buyer gains mainly],
  [a higher rainfall],
  [free seed],
  [a better price through bulk selling],
  [cheaper land]
)

#mcq(39, [The chief characteristic of peasant farming is],
  [small scale, family labour and subsistence orientation],
  [dependence on irrigation],
  [large scale and hired labour],
  [ownership by government]
)

#mcq(40, [Which of these best explains why agriculture is called an art as well as a science?],
  [it requires judgement applied to a particular field and season],
  [it has no tested principles],
  [it is practised only by artists],
  [it needs no knowledge at all]
)

